{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvqGnPJhYXx3vcKjYRjj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CUp5BbHicSLt6ZpJufMgcU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; cp paper.tex revisions/paper_before_repair_round_02b.tex; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper.tex'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1,(s.count(a),a[:60])\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"However, a static first-order influence ranking with refit bisection reaches every one of these budgets, so the more elaborate search we studied adds no measurable gain, and the crowd-versus-sports contrast\",\n\"However, the evaluator's recorded influence-only reference (whose construction we could not verify) matched the studied configuration's budget in all six held-out cases, so these data show no measured gain from the additional search machinery, and the crowd-versus-sports contrast\")\nrep(\"(iii) A one-shot influence ranking with refit bisection already attains every budget; the additional search machinery produced no measured improvement.\",\n\"(iii) The evaluator's recorded influence-only reference matched the studied configuration's budget in every held-out case; we could not verify how that reference is constructed, and the held-out data show no measured improvement from the additional search machinery.\")\nrep(\"(3) A negative result: first-order influence ordering with exact-refit bisection matches the more elaborate configuration everywhere we measured.\",\n\"(3) A negative result: the evaluator's recorded influence-only reference, whose construction is unverified, matches the studied configuration's budget in every held-out case.\")\nrep(\" and show it on published applied analyses. Our setting\",\" for statistical conclusions. Our setting\")\nrep(\"Unlike an approximation-only metric, we accept a removal set only after an exact refit reverses the pair.\",\"We accept a removal set only after an exact refit reverses the pair.\")\nrep(\"Their setting is adversarial and allows an actor to add votes, whereas ours is a deletion-only perturbation checked by exact refit, with no adversary model, so the two are complementary rather than comparable and we do not compare numbers.\",\n\"Our setting is a deletion-only perturbation checked by exact refit, with no adversary model, and we do not compare numbers with that work.\")\nrep(\"So the re-linearisation, the leverage correction and the polish gave no measured reduction on these cases. The same holds on development tables (Section~\\\\ref{sec:dev}). A single static ranking by first-order influence followed by exact-refit bisection is therefore enough to reach every budget we report, and the budgets can be viewed as properties of that simple procedure's output rather than of the more elaborate one. Opponent\",\n\"On these cases the studied configuration therefore shows no measured reduction relative to the evaluator's influence-only reference. Because the construction of that reference is not verified (Section~\\\\ref{sec:method_comp}), we do not conclude that a static influence ranking alone suffices, nor that the re-linearisation, leverage correction and polish contributed nothing; we conclude only that the recorded budgets coincide. On the development tables only aggregates are recorded: the studied configuration's aggregate score of 0.4993 equals the logged aggregate influence-only reference score of 0.4993 (Section~\\\\ref{sec:dev}), and no per-case development budgets are recorded. Opponent\")\nrep(\"\\\\subsection{Comparators and validity controls}\",\"\\\\subsection{Comparators and validity controls}\\\\label{sec:method_comp}\")\nrep(\"Our reading of B2 as one static first-order influence ranking followed by exact-refit prefix bisection, i.e.\\\\ step (a) above without leverage correction, re-linearisation or polishing, is consistent with the inspected source of the starting baseline (Section~\\\\ref{sec:dev}) but is an interpretation, not a verified fact.\",\n\"B2's construction is therefore unverified; in particular we do not assert that it equals step (a) above, and we draw no conclusion that depends on that reading.\")\nrep(\"The evidence does not record which gate criteria\",\"The evidence does not record which gate criteria\") if False else None\nrep(\"and the finding that more elaborate search did not reduce them is a statement about the three configurations tried, not about the minimum.\",\n\"and the absence of a measured reduction relative to the evaluator's influence-only reference is a statement about the recorded comparison, not about the minimum.\")\nrep(\"The studied configuration equals influence-only removal in every case, and\",\"The studied configuration's budgets equal the recorded influence-only reference in every case, and\")\nrep(\"A one-shot influence ranking plus bisection over exact refits certifies small reversal budgets on tables of this size in seconds on a CPU. A reported\",\"The studied configuration's recorded held-out evaluation episodes took about 4.5 s each. A reported\")\nrep(\"A static first-order influence ranking matched the more elaborate search everywhere, so we claim a measurement and not a better method.\",\n\"The evaluator's recorded influence-only reference matched the studied configuration's budgets everywhere (its construction is unverified), so we claim a measurement and not a better method.\")\nrep(\"Evaluating one candidate on the held-out tables takes seconds on a CPU (4.5 s per recorded episode here).\",\"The recorded held-out evaluation episodes of the studied configuration took 4.45 s and 4.51 s each; the hardware is not recorded.\")\nrep(\"\\\\subsection{The studied configuration equals influence-only removal}\",\"\\\\subsection{Studied configuration versus the influence-only reference}\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"static\\|one-shot\\|equals influence\\|CPU\\|simple procedure\" paper.tex"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3378,"cache_read_input_tokens":71435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3378},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13d94285-5611-4acf-b46b-45a0ef63f49b","uuid":"3ccea1ac-bca6-419c-abc6-2aa83d52e13c","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:34:36.446Z","request_id":"req_011CgvqGmVET2y97gViqWUF1"}
